      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Schedule L, Part V Supplemental Information</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Schedule L, Part IV, Line 1. The organization contracted with the Law Offices of Spojmie Nasiri, PC for legal services during 2023 through 2024. This constitutes a transaction with an interested person, as Spojmie Nasiri, who owns the law practice, serves as a director of the organization. To ensure compliance with Treasury Regulation 53.4958-6 and the organization's conflict of interest policy, the Board of Directors evaluated the proposed compensation. After consulting with legal counsel, the matter was brought to the Board for review. The Board assessed the contractor's qualifications, experience, and expertise relevant to the legal work required. The Board deliberated on the scope of legal services and the value of the contractor's expertise to the organization. Following discussion, the Board voted and approved compensation that represented fair market value for the services rendered. This determination considered the quality and scope of services provided, the contractor's qualifications, and prevailing market rates for comparable legal work. The Board's decision was recorded in the official meeting minutes, documenting the review, deliberation, and approval process. The organization maintains documentation of this evaluation and the Board's rationale in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleL>
